\title{Pairing a module with its dual}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [complex paired coefficient](fdip-00IS) uses a module
and its dual, rather than a chosen volume on either one.
The [finite exterior polynomial](fdip-00TF) is now available
over a ring. Can the same dual pairing specify the top
coefficient there, including when a quadratic kernel is singular?}
